##############################################################################
# WHAT BELONGS ON GITHUB -- the rule (set by STAiNLESS, 2026-07-28)
#
# Track a file only if it is one of:
#   1. vanilla RetroFE, inherited from upstream
#   2. a new or altered engine file
#   3. something a public user needs
#   4. something a PR needs
#
# Everything else -- AI session state, agent tooling, internal roadmaps and
# our own process docs -- is LOCAL TO THIS MACHINE and never pushed. Those
# files still live on disk and still work; they are simply not tracked.
#
# Do not re-add any of these on the argument that tracking makes them survive
# a fresh clone or get inherited by new branches. That is an internal
# convenience, and it is exactly what this rule rejects: the public fork
# should read as RetroFE plus our changes, nothing else.
##############################################################################

# AI session state and agent tooling -- local only
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
HANDOVER.md
reflections.json
.vscode/
build.log
nul
.mcp.json
Scripts/mcp-servers/
Scripts/check_branch_ready.ps1
Scripts/test_fixture.ps1

# docs/ is deliberately PARTIALLY tracked, on the same rule.
# TRACKED -- documentation a public user of a shipped feature needs:
#   docs/RetroFE/Settings-Menu-Reboot-Restore.md
#     (the only written record of the launcher "reboot = yes" property
#      anywhere, upstream included -- rule 3)
# IGNORED below -- internal roadmaps, design blueprints, our git procedure,
# and upstream reference material that can simply be re-downloaded.
docs/*.md
docs/RetroFE_Wiki/
docs/RetroFE/retrofe_clean_manual.md
docs/RetroFE/retrofe_knowledge_base.md
docs/RetroFE/*.pdf
docs/RetroFE/RetroFE Modernization and Performance.md
docs/RetroFE/Git-Operating-Procedure.md
docs/RetroFE/Layout-Hot-Reload-Blueprint.md

# Rust build artifacts (RustCore/target reaches 2+ GB with bundled DuckDB)
RetroFE/Source/RustCore/target/

# Shell-redirect debris, e.g. unquoted `pip install requests>=2.31.0`
=*

